From 99972e6b5ad9e3dddd2b85b401fe0a758cc16a70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bartimoussmith-oss <bartimoussmith-oss@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 04:19:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix(a11y): separate adjacent labels; give /transcripts/
 rows a layout

/transcripts/ rendered every row as one run-on line (date, title, file
name and back-link with no separator, visually and in each link's
accessible name) because the row link moved inside
.seo-transcript-link-group and the '.seo-archive-links>li>a' column rule
stopped matching. Adds the missing layout rules.

Elsewhere the markup was already semantic (dl/dt/dd, lists, labelled
navs) and browsers separated it by layout, but tag-stripping extractors
merged neighbours into strings like 'Official agendacheyennecity.org',
'Archive documents0' and '2026City Council5 files'. Adds explicit
whitespace between sibling elements on the archive, meeting, transcript
and shell templates. Whitespace-only nodes are not rendered in flex/grid
containers, so those layouts are unchanged (verified box-for-box).

MyNewSpace: headings, definition cells and friend links joined inline
runs ('About Meread-only', 'Caspercity'); two sentences lost the space
after an inline tag in the exported HTML ('Arenawindow',
'frame-ancestorsthat').

Adds tests/text-separation.mjs (static tag-strip audit plus a browser
pass over accessible names) and runs it in CI after the smoke tests. It
fails with 59 findings on 2a741e6 and passes here.
